 and just some flat  out errors for instance Revere was not  standing in Charlestown waiting to see  the two lights you know the old north  church yeah he hung or he had someone  hang those lights but they weren't for  him he knew for sure what was going on  he was enroute to Charlestown to get on  a horse and do the ride so that's one  element that's just completely mythic  and the other I think several other  historians have talked about this  already but the simple fact that he  wasn't you know alone there was of  course William Dawes there were other  writers as well in fact the the moment  the word began getting out it started  going everywhere immediately there's  just this sort of disorganized rush to  to get the word out and and that was  definitely something that you don't get  out of the you know the old story now  this is not your first book what drew  you to this material or don't reveal the  first book i did was about drugs and the  second book i did was about the size of  government and in reality Revere story  overlaps strangely pretty much 141 yeah  you know smuggling turns out to be a  huge story and the founding of our  country the tax laws and the regulations  the Navigation Acts they were called  that governed commerce and uniting the  colonies were floated by smugglers and  not just you know ragtag guys rich  gentle Brook smuggled and including  Revere uh well he is the people in his  circle definitely he actually did do  some smuggling after the Revolution in  fact against the government he helped  create yes there were tools that he  wanted and needed and there was a law  banning trade with England more tools  and so he just had them brought over  anyway right so it's like ordering from  amazon UK or so pretty much yeah so that  was one element that i was i knew a  little bit about because as I had was  studying the the drug war  the Fourth Amendment stuff came up and  that obviously leads to the writs of  assistance and as you start studying 